< E < A < B$","$D < B < E < A < C$","$D < C < E < A < B$","$C < D < E < B < A$"],"answer":1,"answers":[1],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<blockquote><p>Nitration is an electrophilic aromatic substitution reaction. The $+ M$~effect increases the rate of nitration whereas the $- M$~effect decreases the rate of nitration.</p><p>$- {NO}_{2} ( - M ) , - Br ( + Mbutdominant - I ) and - {CH}_{3} ( + H )$</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-03806b76fe3fd3ee.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 456px; height: 150px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-03806b76fe3fd3ee.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-03806b76fe3fd3ee.png\"></p><p>$- {NO}_{2}$ is strongly deactivating</p><p>$- Br,$ deactivating</p><p>$- {CH}_{3},$ activating group</p><p>$D < B < E < A < C$</p></blockquote>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4c"},{"id":"qz_69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284568","_quizrrId":"69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284568","q":"<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-b9c7e51cf951bf4e.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 558px; height: 162px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-b9c7e51cf951bf4e.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-b9c7e51cf951bf4e.png\"></p><p>In the chemical reactions given above& $A$ and $B$ respectively are :</p>","options":["${H}_{3}{PO}_{2}$ and~${CH}_{3}{CH}_{2}Cl$","${CH}_{3}{CH}_{2}OH$~and~${H}_{3}{PO}_{2}$","${H}_{3}{PO}_{2}$ and~${CH}_{3}{CH}_{2}OH$","${CH}_{3}{CH}_{2}Cl$ and~${H}_{3}{PO}_{2}$"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4c"},{"id":"qz_69de4f6f2ee0e063d928456d","_quizrrId":"69de4f6f2ee0e063d928456d","q":"<p>In the given reactions identify $A$ and $B .$</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-1985babf26573642.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 573px; height: 204px;\"/ data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-1985babf26573642.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-1985babf26573642.png\"></p>","options":["$A: 2$–Pentyne $B:$ trans – $2$ – butene","$A: n$ – Pentane $B:$ trans – $2$ – butene","$A: 2$ – Pentyne $B:$ Cis – $2$ – butene","$A: n$ – Pentane $B: Cis – 2$ – butene"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>In palladium-catalyzed hydrogenations of alkynes, the Lindlar catalyst facilitates the addition of hydrogen to the alkyne to afford the corresponding alkene. When this catalyst is used, the addition of the hydrogen substituent always proceeds via syn addition (addition of the substituent on the same side of the bond).</p><p>But$- 2 -$yne when treated with sodium in liquid ammonia gives trans$- 2 -$butene. The reaction of alkyne with sodium in liquid ammonia produces sodamide in the process converting alkynes to alkenes. Mechanism of Birch Reduction: -Sodium in liquid ammonia produces solvated electrons.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-e16fd156fa5280d6.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 800px; height: 372px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-e16fd156fa5280d6.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-e16fd156fa5280d6.png\"></p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4c"},{"id":"qz_69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284572","_quizrrId":"69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284572","q":"<p>In the following given reaction &#39;$A$&#39; is</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-5c3f26099c27fa43.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 411px; height: 130px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-5c3f26099c27fa43.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-5c3f26099c27fa43.png\"></p>","options":["<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-6b02e7dbf5a7c078.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 123px; height: 134px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-6b02e7dbf5a7c078.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-6b02e7dbf5a7c078.png\">","<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-d22b9ab4a275f900.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 140px; height: 150px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-d22b9ab4a275f900.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-d22b9ab4a275f900.png\">","<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-75df450fdc84766a.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 197px; height: 150px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-75df450fdc84766a.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-75df450fdc84766a.png\">","<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-7ad4e08952db89aa.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 187px; height: 142px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-7ad4e08952db89aa.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-7ad4e08952db89aa.png\">"],"answer":2,"answers":[2],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>In the positive part of the addendum added to the alkene according to Markonikov&#39;s rule. A tertiary carbocation is generated undergo ring expansion as five membered rings is more stable than four membered rings.</p><p></p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-992d6e205e460158.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 625px; height: 270px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-992d6e205e460158.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-992d6e205e460158.png\"></p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4c"},{"id":"qz_69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284577","_quizrrId":"69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284577","q":"The correct order of heat of combustion for following alkadienes is:<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fjee_main%252Fd1e15b22-c890-4014-b194-d34adb242a00-3JJ.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=qxfig138\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 96px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-34d5e2f938361a09.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-34d5e2f938361a09.png\">","options":["\\left(a\\right) < \\left(b\\right) <  \\left($c\\right)$","\\left(a\\right) &lt; \\left(c\\right) &lt;  \\left($b\\right)$","\\left(c\\right) &lt; \\left(b\\right) &lt;  \\left($a\\right)$","\\left(b\\right) &lt; \\left(c\\right) &lt;  \\left($a\\right)$"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fjee_main%252F3JJ.PNG%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=qxfig138\" style=\"width: 459px; height: 142px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-7ed49085bc36d6a4.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-7ed49085bc36d6a4.png\"><br /><br />$∴$ Generally trans is more stable than cis form.<br /><br />Heat of combustion $( \\text{HOC} ) ∝ \\dfrac{1}{\\text{Stability}}$<br /><br />Stability : a &gt; b &gt; c<br /><br />HOC : c &gt; b &gt; a","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4c"},{"id":"qz_69de4f6f2ee0e063d928457c","_quizrrId":"69de4f6f2ee0e063d928457c","q":"For the following sequence of reactions, the correct products are :<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-7f8b57b8b5811457.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 399px; height: 117px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-7f8b57b8b5811457.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-7f8b57b8b5811457.png\">","options":["<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-d460b5393361e026.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 332px; height: 136px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-d460b5393361e026.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-d460b5393361e026.png\">","<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-4179366632ef3036.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 342px; height: 144px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-4179366632ef3036.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-4179366632ef3036.png\">","<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-a91d54d954e913a3.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 328px; height: 123px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-a91d54d954e913a3.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-a91d54d954e913a3.png\">","<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-8f8825b581cdcf9e.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 334px; height: 135px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8f8825b581cdcf9e.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8f8825b581cdcf9e.png\">"],"answer":3,"answers":[3],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>In first step, bromination takes place which reacts with magnesium metal to form Grignard&#39;s reagent. This reagent generates very strong base which abstracts acidic hydrogen from methanol to produce benzene.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-8e4802c793eefa45.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 808px; height: 153px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8e4802c793eefa45.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8e4802c793eefa45.png\"></p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4c"},{"id":"qz_69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284631","_quizrrId":"69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284631","q":"The total number of monobromo derivatives formed by the alkanes with molecular formula ${C}_{5}{H}_{12}$ is (excluding stereo isomers)","options":["","","",""],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<blockquote><p>The Alkanes and their mono bromo dervative are as given below,</p><p>There are three alkanes possible with the formula${C}_{5}{H}_{12}$,</p><p>n-pentane, iso-pentane and neo-pentane.</p><p>And identify the possible mono bromo derivatives formed by each isomer.</p><p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fjee_main%252Fda9ffa52-6ca6-4163-b8c0-bdd102df3d10-image.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=qxfig138\" style=\"width: 524px; height: 280px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-c6ebefab6bed7a84.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-c6ebefab6bed7a84.png\"></p></blockquote>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4c"},{"id":"qz_69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284636","_quizrrId":"69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284636","q":"The number of sigma bonds in& <img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-97d58744c1cdd6be.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 261px; height: 79px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-97d58744c1cdd6be.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-97d58744c1cdd6be.png\">& is _______.","options":["","","",""],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-be26a74d3dd9b4b1.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 227px; height: 103px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-be26a74d3dd9b4b1.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-be26a74d3dd9b4b1.png\"></p><p>Numbers of $\\sigma$ bonds $= 10$</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4c"},{"id":"qz_69de4f6f2ee0e063d928463b","_quizrrId":"69de4f6f2ee0e063d928463b","q":"In the following sequence of reactions the maximum number of atoms present in molecule ‘ $C$ ’ in one plane is_______<br />$A\\overset{Redhot}{\\mathop{\\to}_{Cutube}}B\\overset{C{H}_{3}Cl\\left(1 . eq\\right)}{\\mathop{\\to}_{AnhydrousAlC{l}_{3}}}C$<br />(A is a lowest molecular weight alkyne)","options":["","","",""],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-8e26017c0dad179c.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8e26017c0dad179c.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8e26017c0dad179c.png\"><br />Number of atoms in one plane = $13$","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4c"},{"id":"qz_69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284640","_quizrrId":"69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284640","q":"Number of alkanes obtained on electrolysis of a mixture of ${CH}_{3}COONa$ and ${C}_{2}{H}_{5}COONa$ is_____.","options":["","","",""],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>An aqueous solution of sodium or potassium salt of carboxylic acid is electrolysed in this reaction, resulting in the dissociation of the salt into a carboxylate ion and sodium or potassium ions. </p><p>The total number of different alkanes are formed when the following mixture is subjected to electrolysis:</p><p>${CH}_{3}COONa  \\left(aq\\right)and{C}_{2}{H}_{5}COONa \\left($aq\\right)$ </p><p>In this ethane, butane and propane are formed.</p><p>${CH}_{3}COONa \\to \\overset{∙}{C}{H}_{3}$</p><p>${C}_{2}{H}_{5}COONa \\to \\overset{∙}{C}2{H}_{5}$</p><p>$2\\overset{∙}{C}2{H}_{5} \\to {CH}_{3} - {CH}_{2} - {CH}_{2} - {CH}_{3}$</p><p>$2C\\overset{∙}{H}3 \\to {CH}_{3} - {CH}_{3}$</p><p>$\\overset{∙}{C}{H}_{3} + \\overset{∙}{C}2{H}_{5} \\to {CH}_{3} - {CH}_{2} - {CH}_{3}$</p><p>So, the total number of alkanes formed here will be $3$</p>$","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4c"},{"id":"qz_69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284645","_quizrrId":"69de4f6f2ee0e063d9284645","q":"<p>$17$ mg of a hydrocarbon (M.F. ${C}_{10}{H}_{16}$) takes up $8 . 40mL$ of the ${H}_{2}$~gas measured at $0 ° C$ and $760$ mm of $Hg$. Ozonolysis of the same hydrocarbon yields</p><p>${CH}_{3} - \\mathop{C}_{| |O} - {CH}_{3}, H - \\mathop{C}_{| |O} - H, H - \\mathop{C}_{| |O} - {CH}_{2} - {CH}_{2} - \\mathop{C}_{| |O} - \\mathop{C}_{| |O} - H$</p><p>The number of double bond/s present in the hydrocarbon is</p>","options":["","","",""],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>From the given information:<br />Moles of hydrocarbon& $= \\dfrac{17 \\times {10}^{- 3}}{136} = 1 . 25 \\times {10}^{- 4}$~Mole of ${H}_{2}$~gas</p><p>$⇒ 1 \\times \\dfrac{8 . 40}{1000} = n \\times 0 . 0821 \\times 273$</p><p>$⇒ n = 3 . 75 \\times {10}^{- 4}$</p><p>Thus, moles of hydrogen used to hydrogenate double bonds:</p><p>$= \\dfrac{3 . 75 \\times {10}^{- 4}}{1 . 25 \\times {10}^{- 4}} = 3$</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4c"}]}